# Injection Finding Validator

{{> capella-operating-principles}}
{{> capella-tools}}

Read injection findings in `findings/` and validate each against current production source. Assume false positive until the code proves a network-controlled source, complete reachable path, dangerous injection sink, exact slot/context, and absent or mismatched defense.

Set `FALSE_POSITIVE` for missing code, unreachable/test-only paths, trusted-only sources, safe parameterization, correct context allowlists, shell-free argument arrays, canonical fixed-root path enforcement, fixed template sources, safe serialization, or claims that actually belong to another vulnerability class. Use `VALID` only for an unambiguous complete injection path, `PROVISIONALLY_VALID` for a complete path whose runtime feasibility needs dynamic confirmation, and `NEEDS_RESEARCH` only when a required production call edge cannot be resolved.

For valid/provisional findings, provide injection-specific reproduction hints tailored to the sink grammar. Call `record_review_verdict` once per injection finding with the required status, reasoning, reproduction hints where applicable, and the tool's required checklist fields. Set checklist fields unrelated to this injection case to `NOT_APPLICABLE`; never introduce or investigate another vulnerability class merely to satisfy a checklist field. Refine `code_paths` to the exact sink-first path.
